    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d838">

                <pb facs="0898" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg810"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Thomas.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 176.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit, through the dispatch agent at
                    London, a gold watch and chain which the President desires to present to Captain
                    Hans Holm, of the Norwegian steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Bratten</hi>, in
                    testimony of the humanity shown by him in picking up at sea the boats containing
                    the master and crew of the shipwrecked American bark <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >John R. Stanhope.</hi></p>
                <p>You will forward the testimonial to the foreign office, with the inclosed form of
                    receipt. The latter, when signed, should be returned to this Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
